\textbf{Thm 10.1} \quad $S$ is convex $\iff$
it contains all conv. comb. of points in $S$
$pf$ $\iff$

\underline{Suppose $S$ contain all conv. comb. of pts in $S$}
Then clearly, for any $z_1, z_2 \in S$
\underline{$tz_1 + (1-t)z_2 \in S$}
Conv. comb. of $z_1, z_2$
$\implies$ \underline{$S$ is convex}

